    {
      "id": "0234c0de-0b3d-468f-8689-ca28378eaabd",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -464,
        -1056
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 752,
        "height": 784,
        "content": "## Social Media Campaign Automation Using Google Sheets and Upload Post API\n\nThis workflow automatically publishes scheduled Instagram and Facebook Stories directly from a Google Sheet. It evaluates media formats, uploads photo or video stories, and logs real-time execution results back to your spreadsheet.\n\n## Who’s it for?\nFor social media managers, digital marketers, content creators, and teams who want to automate daily Instagram and Facebook Story publishing directly from Google Sheets without manual intervention.\n\n## How it works\n1. The Schedule Trigger runs automatically every day at 10:00 AM (or a time of your choice).\n2. The workflow fetches pending stories from the `Story` tab in your Google Sheet (filtered by `Status = Ready` and scheduled for the current day).\n3. It detects whether the media is an image or video and routes it to the corresponding Upload Post API node.\n4. The API publishes the story to your connected Instagram Business and Facebook Page accounts.\n5. Execution logs (success timestamps or failure statuses) are automatically recorded back in the `History` tab for audit purposes.\n\n## How to set up\n- Connect your **Google Sheets OAuth2 API** credentials to access your campaign spreadsheet.\n- Connect your **Upload Post API** credentials (linked to your Instagram Business and Facebook Page at https://www.upload-post.com/).\n- Select your target spreadsheet and the `Story` sheet in the `GetContentReady` node.\n- Enter your Facebook Page ID in the `UploadStoryImage` and `UploadStoryVideo` nodes.\n- Test the workflow by setting a sample row to `Ready` in your sheet.\n- Activate the workflow to run on schedule."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d6805b43-f622-42b6-8343-126b861e6e07",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        336,
        -1056
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 832,
        "height": 784,
        "content": "# 📊 GOOGLE SHEETS TEMPLATE GUIDE\n\n> 📥 **Download Sample Template:**  \n> [Click here to download `Spreadshee Template`](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1TSw3JhtrK-9iz95Y_U0gL5a-EvKQqKLSckKwSMuArlM/edit?usp=sharing) *(Use this sample file to quickly set up your Google Sheet)*\nTo ensure the automation works smoothly, your Google Sheet must have two tabs:\n\n### 🟢 Tab 1: `Story` (Your Content Queue)\nFill out these columns whenever you want to schedule a new story:\n\n| Column Header | What to Put Here | Example |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **ID_Story** | A unique code for the story | `STR-001` |\n| **Type** | Specify media type | `Image` or `Video` |\n| **Url** | A public link to your photo/video file | `https://drive.google.com/...` |\n| **Status** | Set to `Ready` when approved for posting | `Ready` or `Draft` |\n| **Day of week**| Formula/Value checking if it posts today | `TRUE` or `FALSE` |\n\n---\n\n### 🔴 Tab 2: `History` (Automatic Execution Log)\nDo not edit this tab manually! The workflow fills this out automatically:\n- **ID_Story**: The ID of the posted content.\n- **Url**: Link to the posted media.\n- **Time_Executed**: Exact time n8n processed the post.\n- **Time_Posted**: Actual upload timestamp from Instagram/Facebook.\n- **Platform**: Platform posted to (`instagram` or `facebook`)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
